1
00:05:45,714 --> 00:05:51,714
What happens when the numbers run out?

2
00:11:31,428 --> 00:11:37,428
Knowing is a action, mystery, science fiction film directed by Alex Proyas.

3
00:17:17,142 --> 00:17:23,142
A teacher opens a time capsule that has been dug up at his son's elementary school; in it are some chilling predictions -- some that have already
occurred and others that are about to -- that lead him to believe his family plays a role in the events that are about to unfold.

4
00:23:02,857 --> 00:23:08,857
John Koestler, played by Nicolas Cage.

5
00:28:48,571 --> 00:28:54,571
Diana Wayland, played by Rose Byrne.

6
00:34:34,285 --> 00:34:40,285
Caleb Koestler, played by Chandler Canterbury.

7
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Phil Bergman, played by Ben Mendelsohn.

8
00:46:05,714 --> 00:46:11,714
Grace Koestler, played by Nadia Townsend.

9
00:51:51,428 --> 00:51:57,428
Cashier, played by Terry Camilleri.

10
00:57:37,142 --> 00:57:43,142
Knowing (stylized as KNOW1NG) is a 2009 science fiction thriller film
directed and co-produced by Alex Proyas and starring Nicolas Cage.

11
01:03:22,857 --> 01:03:28,857
The film, conceived and co-written by Ryne Douglas Pearson, was originally attached to a number of directors
under Columbia Pictures, but it was placed in turnaround and eventually picked up by Escape Artists.

12
01:09:08,571 --> 01:09:14,571
Production was financially backed by Summit Entertainment.

13
01:14:54,285 --> 01:15:00,285
Knowing was filmed in Docklands Studios Melbourne, Australia, using
various locations to represent the film's Boston-area setting.

14
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
The film centers on the discovery of a strange paper filled with numbers and the
possibility that they somehow predict the details of various disasters.

15
01:26:25,714 --> 01:26:31,714
The film was released on March 20, 2009, in the United States.

16
01:32:11,428 --> 01:32:17,428
The DVD and Blu-ray media were released on July 7.

17
01:37:57,142 --> 01:38:03,142
Knowing grossed $186.5 million at the worldwide box office, plus $27.7 million with
home video sales, against an average production budget of $50 million.

18
01:43:42,857 --> 01:43:48,857
It met with mixed reviews, with praise for the acting performances, visual style and
atmosphere, but criticism over some implausibilities and the ending.

19
01:49:28,571 --> 01:49:34,571
The film explores themes of cataclysm, melancholy, code, alien, time capsule.

20
01:55:14,285 --> 01:55:20,285
The tone is mind_bending and thought_provoking and intense.
